/-!
# WAST rows: `test/core/elem.wast`, a linked script answered by one kernel evaluation

Generated by `tools/wasm-wast/gen.py`; do not edit. `script` proves every claim of `cmds`
(`ScriptHolds.of_kernel`, one `decide +kernel` evaluation of `scriptHK`, which allocates the shared
`spectest` table and memory, then validates, links (allocating fresh `spectest` print functions and
globals per import), instantiates and runs every command in order on `KMem` stores, answering
print calls as `Spectest.host`; the claims are about `ByteArray` stores and Core reduction
`Step (profile neverFail) Spectest.host`). Each row `silmaril.wasm_wast.elem.l<line>` is the command at
line `<line>`: `assert_return` (`silmaril.shapes.wasm.wast.host.returns_only`), `assert_trap`
(`….host.traps_only`), `assert_unlinkable` (`….host.unlinkable`) or `assert_uninstantiable`
(`….host.uninstantiable`), after the commands before it (`pre cmds k`). `decodes`: every module of the script is the
decoder's reading of its bytes (not the default `{}` of `getD`), from the same kernel
evaluation. The index fact `cmds[k]? = some …` of a row is checked by `kernel_rfl`.

An `assert_invalid` row (`silmaril.shapes.wasm.wast.validator_rejects`) or binary
`assert_malformed` row (`….decoder_rejects`) is tool-level: silmaril-lean's validator (decoder)
rejects the bytes, by one `decide +kernel` evaluation.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Silmaril.Project.WasmWast.Elem

open Silmaril.Wasm Silmaril.Wasm.Execution.Core Silmaril.Project.Shapes.WasmWastHost

/-- The kernel checker accepts the script, and every module decodes. -/
theorem check : (decodesB && scriptHK Silmaril.Wasm.SingleThreaded.neverFail 100000 cmds) = true := by decide +kernel

/-- Every module of the script is the decoder's reading of its bytes. -/
theorem decodes : decodesB = true := (Bool.and_eq_true_iff.mp check).1

/-- Every claim of the script. -/
theorem script : ScriptHolds Silmaril.Wasm.SingleThreaded.neverFail cmds := .of_kernel (Bool.and_eq_true_iff.mp check).2

